 "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn9le15ob05re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "biographer"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an author who writes the story of someone's life"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Biographers have studied the life of Mozart."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le15ob05aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about fame."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "historian"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person who studies history"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: These questions have been pondered by historians."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le15ob05aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "composer"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " a person who writes music"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: His father was a musician and a composer."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le15ob05aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "genius"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " exceptional intelligence or ability"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Everyone could see that he was a musical genius."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le15ob05aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "prodigy"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " a young person with exceptional abilities"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: He took his five-year-old prodigy on a tour of Europe to play in concerts."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le15ob05aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "ingenuity"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the ability to think of new and clever ways of doing things"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Wolfgang amazed kings, queens, and their courts with his musical ingenuity."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le15ob05aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "venerated"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "extremely respected or honored"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: He is Germany's most venerated musician."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le15ob05aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "acumen"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "skill in a particular subject"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: He was praised by critics and the public for his musical acumen."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le15ob05aud08"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "virtuoso"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person who is extremely skilled, usually at playing an instrument or performing"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: At the age of thirty-five, the great virtuoso died."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le15ob05aud09"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I read about famous celebrity mysteries."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I research a famous person."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I speculate about the past with \u201cmight have, may have and could have.\u201d"}, {"type": "text", "content": "I share my ideas with a partner."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Choose a celebrity who died or disappeared under mysterious circumstances (e.g. Mozart, Elvis, Amelia Earhart)."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Provide some background information on your celebrity."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Explain the death or disappearance by creating list of possible explanations by speculating about the past. (Use <span class=\"italic\">might have</span>, <span class=\"italic\">may have</span> and <span class=\"italic\">could have</span>.)"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Present your ideas to a partner."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Speculation About the Past"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use modals to talk about degrees of certainty and speculate about things in the past.</br> You use them to describe what is definite, probable, possible, or impossible from the speaker's point of view. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use <span class=\"italic\">must</span>, <span class=\"italic\">may</span>, <span class=\"italic\">might</span>, and <span class=\"italic\">could</span> to describe degrees of certainty. </br>You can use modals with the Present Perfect to talk about the possibility of a past event that is not clear in the present context."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:<br/><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Might</span> poison <span class=\"strong\">have been</span> the cause of his death?  </span></br></br> *Notice the structure of a question"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look at the chart for the meanings of modals when speculating about the past:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Modal Phrase </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Meaning </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Must have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It is very likely\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"May have </br>Might have </br> Could have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It is possible\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li><span class=\"italic\">May have </span>has a slightly stronger meaning that <span class=\"italic\">might have</span> or <span class=\"italic\">could have</span>.</li><li> You can add <span class=\"strong\">not</span> to make a negative speculation (<span class=\"italic\">It <span class=\"strong\">may not have been</span> true</span>)."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Ever since, it has been speculated that his death may not have been entirely natural. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Some have suggested that he may have been poisoned by a jealous counterpart, or that he could have been murdered by angry debt-collectors. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "The idea that Mozart might have been murdered is not new."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Passive: The Present Continuous and Present Perfect Tenses"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Present Continuous to talk about an action that is happening at the time of speaking. The action or event is in progress.  </br><span class=\"italic\">Millions of people around the world <span class=\"strong\">are enjoying</span> his music.</span></br></br>You use the Present Perfect to talk about a finished action or event with present consequences. There is a connection between what happened in the past and the present. </br><span class=\"italic\">The great Pushkin <span class=\"strong\">has explored </span>the murder of Mozart.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You often choose the passive form when you want to talk about an action but are not so interested in saying who or what does/did it. Passives without <span class=\"italic\">agents</span> (the doers) are common in biographies."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look at the chart below for the structure of the passive voice."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Name\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Structure\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"am/are/is +  being + past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">His death <span class=\\\"strong\\\">is being contemplated</span> by an inquisitive few.  </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"have/has + been + past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">It <span class=\\\"strong\\\">has been explored</span> in print, by the great Pushkin, and in film, by Milos Forman.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Ever since, it has been speculated that his death may not have been entirely natural."}, {"type": "example", "content": "It is interesting to think that while his music is being enjoyed by millions around the world, his death is being contemplated by an inquisitive few.  "}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "type": "WLC", "questions": [], "img_path": "", "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about fame and work."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about what is being done or what has been done."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can speculate about the past."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " Is classical music still relevant today? Why or why not?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " Which celebrities have died under mysterious circumstances?"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}]}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "Let's take a closer look at the life of Mozart!"}]}, {"template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [1], "questions": [{"responses": [{"correct": 0, "selected": 0, "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}, {"correct": 1, "selected": 0, "id": 1, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}]}], "type": "STI", "id": 1, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "It's a <span class=\"tool-tip\" id=\"tip_1_0\">classic tale</span> of murder and mystery!"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Content"}]}, {"t